{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues","id":162831,"title":"Idigam Chronicle - Crossover Issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T15:46:14-07:00","id":162831,"title":"Idigam Chronicle - Crossover Issues","content":"So I run today mine 5 PCs mages cabal in to fight with relative the same level 5 NPC Forsaken pack. Werewolf were using <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\">new forms damage</a> ( in Gauru +1 from Claws ) and good fight dicepools ( 7-11 dices ), but mages just tear apart 2 NPCs, and only one of the have serious Bashing damage. Only one. Wolves also weren't using Gifts, as I still didn't get to them in my knowledge of <b>Werewolf</b> to make them suitable.<br /> <br /> The <b>Mage</b> PCs ware using <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/314-stop-gap-god-machine-mechanics-for-mage\">Stop Gap rules</a>. The only differences was I didn't use the new Gauru's &quot;Regenerate all&quot; rules on regeneration, only those in <b>Forsaken</b> corebook. PCs were having one 4th dot Arcanum, but the resolution should me a lot more bloodier for Awakaned then.<br /> <br /> Effect was like this - only one mage get a 4 bashes, when cabal destroyed almost all Uratha in fight. Mage's new Shields with 4/1 rules on 4th dot of Arcanum made Awakened unstoppable tanks, even better then werewolves.<br /> <br /> From my little playtest I would advise to give Uratha's claws and jaw attacks something of supernatural armor piercing - damage level is good, but Mages ability to just make &quot;puff the damage&quot;, only need to it is just stay still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2014, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:35:11-07:00","id":162908,"title":"","content":"Huh, I had the opposite experience. My cabal of PCs fought a NPC Pure pack recently, and struggled to make it through the encounter (I've also been using the Stop Gap rules for Mage). The Predator King in the pack had the Strength 3 Gift: Iron Rending (it's houseruled to affect even magical armor) which allowed him to tear through the mage armor. Father Wolf's 4 dot Gift, Savage Rending, combined with Gauru form then proceeded to brutalize my PCs (that said, I've been using the new regeneration rules for Gauru that Stew revealed). The pack's spiritual allies also contributed towards the assault, and my PCs had to beat back a hasty retreat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:00:45-07:00","id":163021,"title":"","content":"Based upon just reading this, it seems like the houseruled Iron Rending going through magical armor made the battle, alongside the regen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T21:35:52-07:00","id":163123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=162908#post162908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Predator King in the pack had the Strength 3 Gift: Iron Rending (it's houseruled to affect even magical armor) which allowed him to tear through the mage armor. Father Wolf's 4 dot Gift, Savage Rending, combined with Gauru form then proceeded to brutalize my PCs (that said, I've been using the new regeneration rules for Gauru that Stew revealed).</div> </div> </div> </div>You house ruled one Gift and it worked only for this one Werewolf. Maybe I'm a bit weird here, but our whole group thought that if Mage Armor is a bit logical from Mage side, then the Werewolf should have &quot;supernatural armor piercer&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Let me give you example:</b><br /> Pack is 5 member in count. Most of them are good in battle - they got 7 dicepool in Brawl on Gauru, even after getting out mages Defence - so they statistically will get 2 successes ( about 30% of success range for dice to roll ). So this mean they should get do about 3 Lethal Damage each round, maybe 4L with some luck. This is logical, as most werewolves would kill people in 1-2 turns, 3 max, like we see on movies.<br /> <br /> But with Armor 4/2 that means that first 4 Damage is totally negligible, and then rest is made in to Bashing Damage. Generally speaking, it makes only very specialized or lucky werewolves to make <b>any</b> harm to mages on 4th dot Armor. And even if Arcanum's 4th Dot should be resaliant bastard, that not un-harmable.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me this is like the thing with vampires flesh all over again - werewolves claws and jaws should be able to omit supernatural Armor, even in some small step. Whatever if it is undead flesh or spell armors. Even a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:15:58-07:00","id":163168,"title":"","content":"I mean, you could just give werewolves' natural weapons Armor Piercing 1 or 2, an be done with it. They'd be so supernaturally strong that they literally rip through armor, mystical or mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T01:05:14-07:00","id":163267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163123#post163123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But with Armor 4/2 that means that first 4 Damage is totally negligible, and then rest is made in to Bashing Damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err...no? Maybe I didn't understand your position, but the rest is still lethal. Plus, even if the damage is totally negated, they still deal 1 bashing.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus, you put 5 &quot;normal people with some stats higher than usual&quot;, no Gifts and a negligible regeneration against a cabal of 4-dot Arcanum mages. Doesn't the why the werewolf died seem evident?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-09-2014, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T01:29:55-07:00","id":163276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163267#post163267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err...no? Maybe I didn't understand your position, but the rest is still lethal. Plus, even if the damage is totally negated, they still deal 1 bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you need to make attack of 5+ Lethal damages to do any real harm to mages in Shields. It is nearly impossible with nowadays rules of high Defense - it would be, statically 15 dicepool on Brawl+Strength, not to count about 3-5 Defense of normal mortal character. So werewolves need dicepools of 18-20 to make real threat to Adept mages, even Disciples - I would say that werewolves are under powered if they need Archmasters-like stats to any really hurt normal Awakened, even if we take bonuses like Gauru form. Don't you?<br /> <br /> And 1 Bashing is laughable - I understand this coming from time to time in combat, when werewolf had bad roll. But every turn is just bad. Mages are mortals, even with they super shields, werewolves should be able to make some real wound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163267#post163267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Plus, you put 5 &quot;normal people with some stats higher than usual&quot;, no Gifts and a negligible regeneration against a cabal of 4-dot Arcanum mages. Doesn't the why the werewolf died seem evident?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm weird, but I think middle experienced werewolf would be able to hurt middle experienced mage in Shield, even little. Gifts should be make them super-effective, just like magic makes the Awakened. The character should be able to hurt one another in this combat.<br /> <br /> I'm agree a bit - I didn't think that Uratha need whole turn regeneration like &quot;all Lethal damage&quot; - it was a bit too harsh, as Mages could only once per scene make Aggravated damage without Mastery. I think that good middle ground would Primal Urge number of Lethals in Gauru per turn - it would make real difference but also don't change characters attacks in to something unbeatable.<br /> <br /> Returning to my game session - we got duel one werewolf vs one mage. I imagine that werewolf in Gauru should be able to pass the Shield of Adept mage, only with like 1-2 Lethal per turn. Other way, it's only 1 Bashing for werewolf - and this <b>is</b> sick, that killing machine can't touch even not full mastered mage.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I agree that probably regeneration in Gauru on Lethals=Primal Urge per turn and giving natural weapons Armor Pricing 1 would solve all problems - werewolves could mark the spot, heal enough to make things interesting, and mages most damage will perish with they Shield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2014, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T02:07:08-07:00","id":163300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163276#post163276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you need to make attack of 5+ Lethal damages to do any real harm to mages in Shields. It is nearly impossible with nowadays rules of high Defense - it would be, statically 15 dicepool on Brawl+Strength, not to count about 3-5 Defense of normal mortal character. So werewolves need dicepools of 18-20 to make real threat to Adept mages, even Disciples - I would say that werewolves are under powered if they need Archmasters-like stats to any really hurt normal Awakened, even if we take bonuses like Gauru form. Don't you?<br /> <br /> And 1 Bashing is laughable - I understand this coming from time to time in combat, when werewolf had bad roll. But every turn is just bad. Mages are mortals, even with they super shields, werewolves should be able to make some real wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. Don't misunderstand me, I do agree that Mage Armor is really exaggerated. Mage Defense is even worse, as you don't even get to deal hit. Mage Armor was also exaggerated pre-GMC.<br /> Note though, someone could have fighted in Dalu and used Martial Arts to deal automatic bashing (though they'd need the fourth dot for doing so, as normal bashing would have been turned into nothing, and the 4th dot makes unarmed damage lethal). They could also have tried to grapple them, and then spend all that was necessary to deal damage: once they're grappled, they don't have Defense against you, and you have more dices to deal damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I'm weird, but I think middle experienced werewolf would be able to hurt middle experienced mage in Shield, even little. Gifts should be make them super-effective, just like magic makes the Awakened. The character should be able to hurt one another in this combat. </div> </div> </div>Have you ever played D&amp;D? Without some kind of great advantage (like regeneration, like gifts), a &quot;fighter&quot; cannot beat a &quot;wizard&quot; when the wizard is buffed and prepared. You just throwed a suboptimal character against a super-effective one with the full power-set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm agree a bit - I didn't think that Uratha need whole turn regeneration like &quot;all Lethal damage&quot; - it was a bit too harsh, as Mages could only once per scene make Aggravated damage without Mastery. I think that good middle ground would Primal Urge number of Lethals in Gauru per turn - it would make real difference but also don't change characters attacks in to something unbeatable. </div> </div> </div>You didn't need the full regeneration, but 1 bashing per turn and 1 lethal using Essence is just laughable in GMC. Yes, Primal urge lethal per turn would have been a game-changer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Returning to my game session - we got duel one werewolf vs one mage. I imagine that werewolf in Gauru should be able to pass the Shield of Adept mage, only with like 1-2 Lethal per turn. Other way, it's only 1 Bashing for werewolf - and this <b>is</b> sick, that killing machine can't touch even not full mastered mage. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are great against mortals. You can't expect them to be lethal to a prepared Mage without any kind of help from Gifts.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd give automatic armor piercing to werewolves, I'd rather give them a gift for Armor piercing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just to make you understand why a random &quot;fighter&quot; with no special things oustide of &quot;i have high Weaponry and Strength&quot; is laughable against a prepared mage, I'll give you an anecdote. It's Pre-GMC, but it's still mostly valid to show what I mean.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene:</b> Obrimos Prime 5 , Thyrsus Life 5 mage, True Fae (very high stats, no useful enough Contracts, and of course little to no method of healing damage, just like your werewolf).<br /> Prime mage-&gt; creates a phantasmal armor on the mage, creating a full suit of physical armor at 5. Then, the Thyrsus uses Life to grant himself a Mage Shield. The Thyrsus also had a merit that allowed him to use the highest of Dexterity and Wits for Defense. But that could also be any other kind of defensive effect.<br /> The true fae had about -17 to all attacks, from Defense and Armor. You'd expect a powerful True fae to be able to harm a mage. Well, it didn't happen. His dice pool was a chance die.<br /> After some attacks, the True Fae was first imprisoned with a phantasmal cage (Prime 4), and then when he broke free, he was turned into a slug with Life 4, and stomped on by the Thyrsus' foot. The True fae didn't stand a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T02:08:33-07:00","id":163301,"title":"","content":"Adepts are not &quot;middle experienced&quot; mages, they are a blink away from being Masters. There's a huge gap in efficiency from Disciple (3 dots) to Adept (4 dots). At 4 you get all the buffs, lethal damage spells, transformations, debuffs, etc.<br /> <br /> You should have used Disciples, second or third degree but Disciples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T02:47:25-07:00","id":163313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163300#post163300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever played D&amp;D? Without some kind of great advantage (like regeneration, like gifts), a &quot;fighter&quot; cannot beat a &quot;wizard&quot; when the wizard is buffed and prepared. You just throwed a suboptimal character against a super-effective one with the full power-set.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are great against mortals. You can't expect them to be lethal to a prepared Mage without any kind of help from Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage with Shield isn't &quot;buffed and prepared&quot; - it's just basic, most fundamental preparation. We don't go here for something like basic &quot;Honing the form&quot;, Matter Enhanced vest and all other variant magic that Arcana can get it - like Gifts can get on werewolves. Shield ( and Mage Sight) is almost as fundamental to life of being mage, like regeneration and shapeshifting is for werewolves.<br /> <br /> I would say that both races should be able to make harm to each other if werewolf in in Gauru and mage is having Shield. Above this, it's true arms race with Gifts and Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163300#post163300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't need the full regeneration, but 1 bashing per turn and 1 lethal using Essence is just laughable in GMC. <b>Yes, Primal urge lethal per turn would have been a game-changer</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in one matter we agree - maybe <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> devs will read this recommendation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163300#post163300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd give automatic armor piercing to werewolves, I'd rather give them a gift for Armor piercing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Armor Piercing solves a lot of problems with crossovers, like vampires flesh, mages shields, or even is logical in game, with werewolves piercing mortals shields and Kevlar vests with claws. And it isn't very big boost, enough to make small, but real difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163300#post163300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make you understand why a random &quot;fighter&quot; with no special things oustide of &quot;i have high Weaponry and Strength&quot; is laughable against a prepared mage, I'll give you an anecdote. It's Pre-GMC, but it's still mostly valid to show what I mean.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene:</b> Obrimos Prime 5 , Thyrsus Life 5 mage, True Fae (very high stats, no useful enough Contracts, and of course little to no method of healing damage, just like your werewolf).<br /> Prime mage-&gt; creates a phantasmal armor on the mage, creating a full suit of physical armor at 5. Then, the Thyrsus uses Life to grant himself a Mage Shield. The Thyrsus also had a merit that allowed him to use the highest of Dexterity and Wits for Defense. But that could also be any other kind of defensive effect.<br /> The true fae had about -17 to all attacks, from Defense and Armor. You'd expect a powerful True fae to be able to harm a mage. Well, it didn't happen. His dice pool was a chance die.<br /> After some attacks, the True Fae was first imprisoned with a phantasmal cage (Prime 4), and then when he broke free, he was turned into a slug with Life 4, and stomped on by the Thyrsus' foot. The True fae didn't stand a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>eWe talk here about Mages that have powers even more powerfull like Werewolves with 5 Dot Gifts - of course they will eat him. Rather true comparison would be putting one mage on with one Arcanum on 5th Dot with on w Werewolf with 3 Gifts at 5th dot - it would be about right leve<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163301#post163301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adepts are not &quot;middle experienced&quot; mages, they are a blink away from being Masters. There's a huge gap in efficiency from Disciple (3 dots) to Adept (4 dots). At 4 you get all the buffs, lethal damage spells, transformations, debuffs, etc.<br /> <br /> You should have used Disciples, second or third degree but Disciples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the combat experienced, Primal Urge 3-4 Uratha should be able to make some real damage to them - like a Lethal 2-3 per mage. Not defeat them, but true massacre of wolves shouldn't come in to being. Without taking Gifts in account, that should give a balance factor to make it a bit 50:50.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2014, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T02:59:43-07:00","id":163316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage with Shield isn't &quot;buffed and prepared&quot; - it's just basic, most fundamental preparation. We don't go here for something like basic &quot;Honing the form&quot;, Matter Enhanced vest and all other variant magic that Arcana can get it - like Gifts can get on werewolves. Shield ( and Mage Sight) is almost as fundamental to life of being mage, like regeneration and shapeshifting is for werewolves. </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course. But just like &quot;mage armor and big physical armor&quot; was just enough preparation to kill the True Fae (which was actually pretty good at fighting), &quot;mage shield&quot; is enough for &quot;normal people with claws with meaningless healing&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, the combat experienced, Primal Urge 3-4 Uratha should be able to make some real damage to them. Not defeat them, but true massacare iof wolves shouldn't come in to being. Without taking Gifts in account, that should give a balance factor to make it a bit 50:50. </div> </div> </div>Primal urge alone is mostly meaningless to Werewolves. Yay, longer Gauru. Except it doesn't influence the outcome if you die the in the first three turns. Yay, more Essence. You only get more Essence to heal yourself, and some more Essence per turn, which is not that big of a boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T04:00:11-07:00","id":163363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163316#post163316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal urge alone is mostly meaningless to Werewolves. Yay, longer Gauru. Except it doesn't influence the outcome if you die the in the first three turns. Yay, more Essence. You only get more Essence to heal yourself, and some more Essence per turn, which is not that big of a boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this why should regernation being based on this - Primal Urge becomes more important in to combat when it's number of your healing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:02:55-07:00","id":163402,"title":"","content":"In the current IC drafts there are multiple ways for Uratha to gain Armour Piercing on their natural weapons. Werewolves have a *lot* of 'bolt-on' combat upgrades available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:13:45-07:00","id":163416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163402#post163402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the current IC drafts there are multiple ways for Uratha to gain Armour Piercing on their natural weapons. Werewolves have a *lot* of 'bolt-on' combat upgrades available.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:20:07-07:00","id":163441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163402#post163402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the current IC drafts there are multiple ways for Uratha to gain Armour Piercing on their natural weapons. Werewolves have a *lot* of 'bolt-on' combat upgrades available.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this multiple options I hope the aren't all specific Gifts? But rather like &quot;when using Essence it can be burn to make Armour Piercing on natural weapons&quot;. Or maybe Totems boons? I look for something very general, so most ( if not all ) Uratha could use it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:24:13-07:00","id":163446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163441#post163441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With this multiple options I hope the aren't all specific Gifts? But rather like &quot;when using Essence it can be burn to make Armour Piercing on natural weapons&quot;. Or maybe Totems boons? I look for something very general, so most ( if not all ) Uratha could use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like the Vampire Merit that lets their claws do Agg damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T07:16:00-07:00","id":163556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163441#post163441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With this multiple options I hope the aren't all specific Gifts? But rather like &quot;when using Essence it can be burn to make Armour Piercing on natural weapons&quot;. Or maybe Totems boons? I look for something very general, so most ( if not all ) Uratha could use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the methods for getting Armour Piercing is easily available to all Uratha, but Uratha do not have Armour Piercing built into their 'baseline' capabilities. There's a Facet that also gives it and it's not exactly hard to access for a combat-specced werewolf.<br /> <br /> If I am doing the calculations right, an (admittedly high-Glory) werewolf can hit something like AP 7.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that against armour that comes from a physical item, werewolves have further options and powers for attacking that directly. Obviously this doesn't help much against the core Mage Armour that mages shield themselves with, but it's handy for things like phantasmally conjured stuff and Matter-enhanced body armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:12:57-07:00","id":163642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163556#post163556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the methods for getting Armour Piercing is easily available to all Uratha, but Uratha do not have Armour Piercing built into their 'baseline' capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we got a Merit for this kind of things, as I see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cool, I before shoved the proposed Merit of &quot;animal defense&quot; in bestial forms in to core template, I will shove this one also. I run a mostly Mage crossovers, so Wolves can get a bit love for them too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163556#post163556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Facet that also gives it and it's not exactly hard to access for a combat-specced werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool to know, my Rahu NPCs will love it, probably. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163556#post163556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am doing the calculations right, an (admittedly high-Glory) werewolf can hit something like AP 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me really glad - and terrified, in the same moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like that there are many ways for AP as this seem a bit of small part from werewolf popculture that was a bit left one before. Now I can make terrifying everything ravenous beast, finally!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163556#post163556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that against armour that comes from a physical item, werewolves have further options and powers for attacking that directly. Obviously this doesn't help much against the core Mage Armour that mages shield themselves with, but it's handy for things like phantasmally conjured stuff and Matter-enhanced body armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very happy that mages Arcana capebilites are being in to consideration - it will make running crossover games easier. <br /> <br /> Really, you convinced me that Uratha's powers and crossover issues are in right hands! Or maybe paws, would be more accurate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:24:33-07:00","id":163670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163300#post163300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever played D&amp;D? Without some kind of great advantage (like regeneration, like gifts), a &quot;fighter&quot; cannot beat a &quot;wizard&quot; when the wizard is buffed and prepared. You just throwed a suboptimal character against a super-effective one with the full power-set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, and this is patently not true. Wizards are tough, but they are not nigh invulnerable, even in D&amp;D. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:25:19-07:00","id":163671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163446#post163446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe something like the Vampire Merit that lets their claws do Agg damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the Gift - <b>Savage Rending</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:50:23-07:00","id":163806,"title":"","content":"OFFTOPIC<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163670#post163670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have, and this is patently not true. Wizards are tough, but they are not nigh invulnerable, even in D&amp;D. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ. Well, it depends on how many books you involve. Wizards and clerics can build a really high value of AC, Saving throws and blanket immunities. Tome of Battle isn't going to help you either.<br /> <b>In core</b><br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Guess you don't mind being non-magical. (Mord's Disjunction).&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have 70+ AC. (shapechange + buffs, easily reachable)&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You are a grappler. Too bad I've a ring of free movement.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I act twice per turn (chocker [Monster Manual]) and have high Initiative. (Shapechange)&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Guess you don't mind if a bulk of elder earth elementals grapple you.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad my CL is 45, thanks to being a red wizard, despite being only a 20th level character. (Thanks to Gate you can summon a creature with double your caster level in Hit Dices. Good morning Old Prismatic Dragon (and that's only 58 HD, but it's also CR 48. Or what about an Elder Titan? http://www.d20srd.org/srd/epic/monsters/titanElder.htm&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Out of core...</b><br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn with your sword. Too bad I'm immune to metal. http://dndtools.eu/spells/spell-compendium--86/greater-ironguard--3925/.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have Evasion, an anti-magic field and I can cast in anti-magic fields. <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/spells/book-of-exalted-deeds--52/starmantle--13/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/spells/book-of-ex...tarmantle--13/</a> , <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/feats/complete-adventurer--54/extraordinary-spell-aim--1057/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/feats/complete-ad...ell-aim--1057/</a> or <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/feats/players-guide-to-faerun--22/initiate-mystra--3776/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/feats/players-gui...-mystra--3776/</a> &quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have Celerity + Time stop + delayed blast soundball x3 and a metamagic rod of empowerment (thank you Elemental mastery).&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Hope you have a ghost weapon (blink, greater)&quot;<br /> &quot;Really impressive! You have an Anti-magic field! Too bad I can cast in it/I have a contingency for that&quot;<br /> &quot;Really impressive! You deal 1000 damage. All wasted against my contingent Otiluke Elastic Sphere&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-09-2014, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:14:59-07:00","id":163817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163806#post163806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OFFTOPIC<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I beg to differ. Well, it depends on how many books you involve. Wizards and clerics can build a really high value of AC, Saving throws and blanket immunities. Tome of Battle isn't going to help you either.<br /> <b>In core</b><br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Guess you don't mind being non-magical. (Mord's Disjunction).&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have 70+ AC. (shapechange + buffs, easily reachable)&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You are a grappler. Too bad I've a ring of free movement.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I act twice per turn (chocker [Monster Manual]) and have high Initiative. (Shapechange)&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Guess you don't mind if a bulk of elder earth elementals grapple you.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad my CL is 45, thanks to being a red wizard, despite being only a 20th level character. (Thanks to Gate you can summon a creature with double your caster level in Hit Dices. Good morning Old Prismatic Dragon (and that's only 58 HD, but it's also CR 48. Or what about an Elder Titan? http://www.d20srd.org/srd/epic/monsters/titanElder.htm&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Out of core...</b><br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn with your sword. Too bad I'm immune to metal. http://dndtools.eu/spells/spell-compendium--86/greater-ironguard--3925/.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have Evasion, an anti-magic field and I can cast in anti-magic fields. <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/spells/book-of-exalted-deeds--52/starmantle--13/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/spells/book-of-ex...tarmantle--13/</a> , <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/feats/complete-adventurer--54/extraordinary-spell-aim--1057/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/feats/complete-ad...ell-aim--1057/</a> or <a href=\"http://dndtools.eu/feats/players-guide-to-faerun--22/initiate-mystra--3776/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dndtools.eu/feats/players-gui...-mystra--3776/</a> &quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Too bad I have Celerity + Time stop + delayed blast soundball x3 and a metamagic rod of empowerment (thank you Elemental mastery).&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, impressive. You deal 1000 damage per turn. Hope you have a ghost weapon (blink, greater)&quot;<br /> &quot;Really impressive! You have an Anti-magic field! Too bad I can cast in it/I have a contingency for that&quot;<br /> &quot;Really impressive! You deal 1000 damage. All wasted against my contingent Otiluke Elastic Sphere&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow - Power game Much?<br /> Often it is as simple as: &quot;Wow, you cast your spell and I resisted it, now suck up 3 attacks that deal enough damage to kill you.&quot; *shrug*<br /> I have seen that scenario play out often enough to say that Wizards can be killed with fairly mundane means and good tactics (My last Warrior, a Champion of Moradin, did not even USE magic items, and the majority of magical opponents never really stood much of a chance). Tactics trump Power trips more often than not (Not accusing you of such things, just pointing out that More Powerz is not a good comparison for tactics).<br /> <br /> Rarely do my games ever get to the point you describe. Mostly because I do not allow it to become a &quot;Players&quot; vs. &quot;GM&quot; power fest. No one cares how big the other's phallus is. *shrug*<br /> <br /> And another thing... Don't beg, its demeaning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-09-2014, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:46:01-07:00","id":163861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163817#post163817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow - Power game Much?<br /> Often it is as simple as: &quot;Wow, you cast your spell and I resisted it, now suck up 3 attacks that deal enough damage to kill you.&quot; *shrug*<br /> I have seen that scenario play out often enough to say that Wizards can be killed with fairly mundane means and good tactics (My last Warrior, a Champion of Moradin, did not even USE magic items, and the majority of magical opponents never really stood much of a chance). Tactics trump Power trips more often than not (Not accusing you of such things, just pointing out that More Powerz is not a good comparison for tactics).<br /> <br /> Rarely do my games ever get to the point you describe. Mostly because I do not allow it to become a &quot;Players&quot; vs. &quot;GM&quot; power fest. No one cares how big the other's phallus is. *shrug*<br /> <br /> And another thing... Don't beg, its demeaning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong. I've passed the phase of true powergaming a long time ago and reverted to a more reasonable optimization level. These are only some few examples of the many. Plus, I'm mostly a DM. I had to actively nerf many spells, and ban some others. Still, most of the time my parties roflstops mildly optimized encounters with a few well places buffs, debuffs or battlefield control spells. The spellcaster player is really good at strategies, and even when not winning initiative (which is rare), he's not going to die suddenly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-09-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:31:36-07:00","id":163896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163671#post163671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like the Gift - <b>Savage Rending</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I never generated enough interest before with Forsaken to take the time to read through the book carefully. Or was too busy trying to upsell Changeling. Or trying to run a mixed supernatural game where all 5 players picked a different template. That was the worst.<br /> <br /> Point is, you're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:42:38-07:00","id":163910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162831-idigam-chronicle-crossover-issues?p=163861#post163861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me wrong. I've passed the phase of true powergaming a long time ago and reverted to a more reasonable optimization level. These are only some few examples of the many. Plus, I'm mostly a DM. I had to actively nerf many spells, and ban some others. Still, most of the time my parties roflstops mildly optimized encounters with a few well places buffs, debuffs or battlefield control spells. The spellcaster player is really good at strategies, and even when not winning initiative (which is rare), he's not going to die suddenly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decently played mages are indeed robust, but I have never seen a Mage as Robust as a Decently put together Warrior. Where they truly shine is in their options, which are vast, and increase with level. Kind of like nWOD mages actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, Most opposition in D&amp;D is not meant to defeat the Players, in my experience. They are there to provide a speed bump to the adventure. Only when you decouple Challenge ratings from the game does a character ever really have to be wary of opposition. I do not use Challenge Ratings, and I never would. Eliminates the feeling of verisimilitude I shoot for (yes, I know, verisimilitude in Fantasy - Go Figure). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-10-2014, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}